WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.353 --> 00:00:01.792
This is Open Orders.

2
00:00:01.792 --> 00:00:06.433
It shows every order you have resting on your exchanges, waiting to fill.

3
00:00:06.433 --> 00:00:10.024
Cyrus reads them straight from each exchange you've connected.

4
00:00:10.695 --> 00:00:13.930
Under the title is the time the list was last updated.

5
00:00:13.930 --> 00:00:17.711
Cyrus checks your exchanges for orders every four minutes in the

6
00:00:17.711 --> 00:00:21.257
background, and straight away whenever you switch accounts.

7
00:00:21.942 --> 00:00:25.828
The heading counts how many orders are open on the accounts you're looking at.

8
00:00:25.828 --> 00:00:29.378
On the right, you can switch between two views: a flow

9
00:00:29.378 --> 00:00:32.730
chart, which is where the page opens, and a table.

10
00:00:33.390 --> 00:00:37.130
The flow chart shows where your money would move if your orders filled.

11
00:00:37.130 --> 00:00:42.316
A sell order moves money out of the coin you're selling and into the one you'd be paid in.

12
00:00:42.316 --> 00:00:44.337
A buy order does the opposite.

13
00:00:45.012 --> 00:00:49.882
On All Exchanges, each account gets its own panel, with its name at the top.

14
00:00:50.608 --> 00:00:52.616
The map reads from left to right.

15
00:00:52.566 --> 00:00:55.079
On the left are coins your orders spend.

16
00:00:55.079 --> 00:01:01.077
Next to each coin is a box for every order, with buy or sell, the amount and the price.

17
00:01:01.077 --> 00:01:04.428
A line then carries on to the coin that order brings in.

18
00:01:05.086 --> 00:01:06.841
Click an order to follow it.

19
00:01:06.791 --> 00:01:09.983
Its line lights up and the rest of the map fades back.

20
00:01:09.983 --> 00:01:13.623
Underneath, Cyrus spells the order out in plain English,

21
00:01:13.623 --> 00:01:16.938
with its status, its type, and when it was placed.

22
00:01:17.615 --> 00:01:22.868
A coin in the middle, like dollars here, is one your orders both pay into and spend.

23
00:01:22.818 --> 00:01:25.943
Its label counts the orders going in and coming out.

24
00:01:25.943 --> 00:01:30.185
The map is often wider than the screen, so drag it to look around.

25
00:01:30.185 --> 00:01:32.392
The buttons above it zoom in and out.

26
00:01:33.061 --> 00:01:38.021
On the far right, a green outline marks a coin your orders only receive.

27
00:01:37.971 --> 00:01:42.971
Under it is roughly how much would arrive if every order flowing into it filled in full.

28
00:01:42.971 --> 00:01:46.668
For dollars and stablecoins, that's shown as a dollar amount.

29
00:01:47.298 --> 00:01:50.533
With four accounts connected, that's a lot of orders.

30
00:01:50.533 --> 00:01:54.256
To focus on one, use the exchange selector at the top.

31
00:01:54.256 --> 00:01:57.102
Let's pick the Robinhood account called Crypto.

32
00:01:57.790 --> 00:02:00.612
Now the chart shows only that account's orders.

33
00:02:00.612 --> 00:02:04.735
The subtitle names the account, and the count drops to match.

34
00:02:05.409 --> 00:02:07.473
Here it's easier to follow the story.

35
00:02:07.473 --> 00:02:12.806
The coins being sold feed into dollars, and dollars feed the coins being bought.

36
00:02:13.478 --> 00:02:15.157
Now let's switch to the table.

37
00:02:15.157 --> 00:02:18.375
It lists the same orders, one row each.

38
00:02:19.050 --> 00:02:24.878
Order ID is the exchange's own reference for the order, and Pair is the market it's on.

39
00:02:24.878 --> 00:02:31.699
Side is buy or sell, in green or red, and Type is the kind of order, such as a limit order.

40
00:02:32.389 --> 00:02:35.132
Price is the price the order is waiting for.

41
00:02:35.132 --> 00:02:40.570
Volume is the full size of the order, and Filled is how much of it has already traded.

42
00:02:41.260 --> 00:02:43.112
Like this Dogecoin buy order.

43
00:02:43.112 --> 00:02:47.872
Part of it has already filled, and the rest is still waiting on the exchange.

44
00:02:48.538 --> 00:02:53.581
Status is what the exchange reports for the order, and Opened is when it was placed.

45
00:02:54.263 --> 00:02:58.459
Switch back to All Exchanges, and the table gains an Exchange column at

46
00:02:58.459 --> 00:03:02.537
the front, so you can always tell which account an order belongs to.

47
00:03:03.220 --> 00:03:07.532
Open Orders is for keeping an eye on things, so there's nothing to change here.

48
00:03:07.532 --> 00:03:11.309
To place new limit orders or cancel existing ones, use

49
00:03:11.309 --> 00:03:14.806
the Limit Orders page, just below in the sidebar.

50
00:03:15.488 --> 00:03:18.177
Your automations can also watch these orders.

51
00:03:18.177 --> 00:03:21.431
A rule can wait for one of them to fill, and then run

52
00:03:21.431 --> 00:03:24.747
an action for you, like a conversion or a withdrawal.

53
00:03:25.443 --> 00:03:29.254
That's Open Orders: every resting order in one place, as a

54
00:03:29.254 --> 00:03:33.066
map of where your money is headed or as a detailed table.

55
00:03:33.066 --> 00:03:35.420
Next, we'll look at limit orders.

